  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.1.6 stable: JS WebTorrent live-swarm interop PASSING + carries the SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.6 tracker-signaling fixes. (1) New `interop_test/js_webtorrent_liveswarm.cs` drives a real Node.js `webtorrent@^2` seeder (via `@roamhq/wrtc`) paired against SpawnDev.WebTorrent C# as the leech through a local SpawnDev.RTC.Server WebSocket tracker: 1 MiB hybrid torrent, real WebRTC offer/answer exchange, SHA-256 byte-identical end-to-end. Closes the \"Pure JS-WebTorrent live interop\" audit gap in `PLAN-BEP52-External-Interop.md`. (2) Transitive dep-bump to SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.6: `TypeInfoResolver` fix unblocks tracker announce serialization under AOT/trimmed/file-based `dotnet run script.cs` hosts (.NET 10), plus empty-Origin bypass on `AllowedOrigins` allowlist unblocks desktop C# / Node.js / curl consumers that don't send Origin headers. (3) Test infrastructure: new in-process `LocalTrackerFixture` removes hub.spawndev.com dependency from desktop tests; superseded `JsInteropTest.cs` deleted in favor of the new `interop_test/js_webtorrent_liveswarm.cs` harness; `RetryCount = 2` added on 7 live-public-swarm tests (Sintel + BEP46 loopback + UseExtension + OnWire); BEP46 loopback ports randomized to avoid TIME_WAIT collisions on retry. PlaywrightMultiTest full sweep **950 pass / 0 fail / 16 skip** in 7m 43s.",
